Subject: Cantor Self Work Physical Update Broker Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 1cb6b870-6ee7-4b29-90e9-86961f0ed9e9
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 5ef3f577-a3f5-46bb-b49c-fa17d08a5765
@ [canonical_uuid] 5f178438-8dad-4d96-be46-66c75b881f1b

& [Claim]
  + complete SWA-04B design formation is necessary before Cantor can truthfully perform its own update
  + separate B0 through B5 commissions are the smallest formation that preserves freshness containment observation acceptance rollback and downstream publication distinctions

& [Support]
  + the current-thread source explicitly requires distinct objective execution verification update and succeeding-SOP authority stages
  + published SWA-04A deliberately stops at representation-only prepared-awaiting-physical-revalidation
  + the source-to-substrate audit finds reusable Phase3A semantics but only formation-level mutation and seal-review candidates
  + historical Phase3B and Phase3C themselves require renewed signatures and physical prerequisites
  + current read-only adapter behavior cannot authorize or establish workspace-write containment

& [AlternativesRejected]
  + direct live writer is rejected because current-interface target-host containment evidence-root review and rollback capabilities are unsigned
  + a pure proposal-only continuation is rejected because it repeats SWA-04A without advancing the missing physical boundary
  + one all-capability broker is rejected because it enables self-review self-rollback self-publication and authority laundering
  + direct SWA-05 commit-push work is rejected because mutation verification and acceptance must precede publication
  + provider-driven work is rejected because the pinned provider is unavailable and SWA-04B must have provider-free fixtures first

& [Counterarguments]
  + [complexity] six stages add machinery; response is that each corresponds to a distinct consequence and authority boundary already required by source and prior evidence
  + [latency] independent observation and review cost time; response is that update correctness and workspace safety are higher consequence than route latency
  + [duplication] Phase3B and Phase3C already describe much of this; response is that they are historical formation-only and do not bind current SWA lineage or current activation facts
  + [no_immediate_feature] formation does not yet write; response is that signing an unproved writer would create false product readiness and block trustworthy self-work later

& [Invalidation]
  + source or predecessor drift
  + capability overlap or metadata-to-handle construction
  + any claim that events prove prevention or writer output proves post-state
  + any activation without current host proof and separate stage signature
  + any rollback cleanup commit push provider self-signature activation or foreign-source inference

& [Decision]
  + complete and publish formation only
  + next separately source B0 pure protocol fixtures
  + keep every physical stage inactive until its exact prerequisites close
